  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research. The team is expanding with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with onboarding on September 10th. An R&D call for ideas to enhance data visualization tools with AI was issued, with a deadline of July 20th. The project reached a milestone with the successful completion of the testing phase, celebrated on October 10th, and achieved an early milestone with a tested prototype for secure file sharing. A total budget of $2M has been approved for research, development, and marketing, with a team meeting scheduled for August 1st to discuss allocations. Additionally, a $15,000 budget for specialized training for coding teams and project managers has been approved, starting next month. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, are being updated to take effect in January."
